type/radio] [:db/add "6ba3c035-d39a-51f4-a80d-e90fd04fd481" :answer-field/choices "a7f4834e-c7db-59b1-b1cb-c29c1c3d6a24"] [:db/add "6ba3c035-d39a-51f4-a80d-e90fd04fd481" :answer-field/choices "0b9bd542-2491-5f93-b519-a4b8c9104142"] [:db/add "6ba3c035-d39a-51f4-a80d-e90fd04fd481" :answer-field/choices "936987e8-463d-56fd-a455-1ecb3a276350"] [:db/add "6ba3c035-d39a-51f4-a80d-e90fd04fd481" :answer-field/choices "aeb56c9c-e96f-5172-8b6e-3ca78254275e"] [:db/add "6ba3c035-d39a-51f4-a80d-e90fd04fd481" :answer-field/choices "78aefd9c-d2c4-5770-a770-20b6ef83e483"] [:db/add "6ba3c035-d39a-51f4-a80d-e90fd04fd481" :answer-field/correct "936987e8-463d-56fd-a455-1ecb3a276350"] [:db/ensure "6ba3c035-d39a-51f4-a80d-e90fd04fd481" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "cd9b0053-2506-5b0c-93ea-34c69732c3f0" :question/id #uuid "cd9b0053-2506-5b0c-93ea-34c69732c3f0"] [:db/add "cd9b0053-2506-5b0c-93ea-34c69732c3f0" :question/problem "The arrows show $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf a$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf b$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf c$. Grid squares have side length one unit.\n\n![](images/ec/ec393bd447e64e9eb013c9334b872c5891a75464462a075324d9f0591c1e12ff.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\mathbf{a}+\\lambda\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$."] [:db/add "cd9b0053-2506-5b0c-93ea-34c69732c3f0" :question/worked-solution "Construct the known component $\\mathbf{a}$ from $O$, ending at $A$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OA} &=1\\,(0, -2)=(0, -2). \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{AC} &=(6, 0).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/94/94de588ace8196f7a159e83013480620ebb7726d2ca173621d402651ebcf0174.png)\n\nCompare the remaining displacement with $\\mathbf{b}$, whose grid displacement is $(4, 0)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Horizontal scale} &=\\frac{6}{4}=\\frac{3}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\\mathbf{b}$. Thus $\\overrightarrow{AC}=\\frac{3}{2}\\mathbf{b}$. By the triangle law,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c} &=\\overrightarrow{OA}+\\overrightarrow{AC} \\\\\n&=\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{3}{2}\\mathbf{b} \\\\\n&=\\mathbf{a}+\\frac{3}{2}\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\\mathbf{b}$ gives $\\lambda=\\frac{3}{2}$."] [:db/add "cd9b0053-2506-5b0c-93ea-34c69732c3f0" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [:db/add "cd9b0053-2506-5b0c-93ea-34c69732c3f0" :question/answer-fields "6ba3c035-d39a-51f4-a80d-e90fd04fd481"] [:db/ensure "cd9b0053-2506-5b0c-93ea-34c69732c3f0" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186096701 :knowledge-point/questions "cd9b0053-2506-5b0c-93ea-34c69732c3f0"] [:db/add "e53d9800-5af1-52f1-b1f1-c62f93104c22" :answer/id #uuid "e53d9800-5af1-52f1-b1f1-c62f93104c22"] [:db/add "e53d9800-5af1-52f1-b1f1-c62f93104c22" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "e53d9800-5af1-52f1-b1f1-c62f93104c22" :answer/value "3"] [:db/ensure "e53d9800-5af1-52f1-b1f1-c62f93104c22" :answer/validate] [:db/add "a628a1dd-2ea2-5120-8179-10046b356f3b" :answer-field/id #uuid "a628a1dd-2ea2-5120-8179-10046b356f3b"] [:db/add "a628a1dd-2ea2-5120-8179-10046b356f3b" :answer-field/key "field-1"] [:db/add "a628a1dd-2ea2-5120-8179-10046b356f3b" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "a628a1dd-2ea2-5120-8179-10046b356f3b" :answer-field/choices "e53d9800-5af1-52f1-b1f1-c62f93104c22"] [:db/add "a628a1dd-2ea2-5120-8179-10046b356f3b" :answer-field/correct "e53d9800-5af1-52f1-b1f1-c62f93104c22"] [:db/ensure "a628a1dd-2ea2-5120-8179-10046b356f3b" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "430ba402-fadf-54f3-838b-fc04d5c73c40" :question/id #uuid "430ba402-fadf-54f3-838b-fc04d5c73c40"] [:db/add "430ba402-fadf-54f3-838b-fc04d5c73c40" :question/problem "The arrows show $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf a$, $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf b$, and $\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\mathbf c$. Grid squares have side length one unit.\n\n![](images/0f/0f345644213f3b78013d06f25e39df9b74ab93a0560ac7611f4b51186c47b905.png)\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$.\n\n$\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}."] [:db/add "430ba402-fadf-54f3-838b-fc04d5c73c40" :question/worked-solution "Construct the known component $\\mathbf{b}$ from $O$, ending at $B$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OB} &=1\\,(0, -3)=(0, -3). \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{BC} &=(-6, 0).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/8a/8a4ecc321f6a818275a9281cc80a82506b9b1a3f6826cbc6dbd011b798895041.png)\n\nCompare the remaining displacement with $\\mathbf{a}$, whose grid displacement is $(-2, 0)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Horizontal scale} &=\\frac{-6}{-2}=3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\\mathbf{a}$. Thus $\\overrightarrow{BC}=3\\mathbf{a}$. By the triangle law,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c} &=\\overrightarrow{OB}+\\overrightarrow{BC} \\\\\n&=\\mathbf{b}+3\\mathbf{a} \\\\\n&=3\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\\mathbf{a}$ gives $\\lambda=3$."] [:db/add "430ba402-fadf-54f3-838b-fc04d5c73c40" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [:db/add "430ba402-fadf-54f3-838b-fc04d5c73c40" :question/answer-fields "a628a1dd-2ea2-5120-8179-10046b356f3b"] [:db/ensure "430ba402-fadf-54f3-838b-fc04d5c73c40" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186096701 :knowledge-point/questions "430ba402-fadf-54f3-838b-fc04d5c73c40"] [:db/ensure 17592186096701 :knowledge-point/validate]]
